                "evidence": "review changes_requested: duetflow/app.py is untouched, so `collect` is still listed in the NOT_YET dict (app.py:21) and wired to cmd_not_yet (app.py:168). Concrete input: after this branch merges, `duetflow collect` prints \"`duetflow collect` arrives in phase 02-collector-schema.\" to stderr and exits 2. collector.collect() is therefore reachable only from tests/test_collector.py and is dead code in the shipped program. This directly breaks docs/ROADMAP.md 02-collector-schema notes (\"The systemd timer is deliberately NOT part of this phase (\u00a78); run Collection manually until 08-timers-notify\") \u2014 there is no manual path to run a Collection \u2014 and docs/PLAN.md \u00a72, which lists `duetflow collect` as one of the five commands app.py exposes. Wire a cmd_collect that opens the db, loads role b's account, obtains a live access token, and calls collector.collect(), and remove `collect` from NOT_YET.; collector.collect() (duetflow/collector.py:14-29) never checks the Collection gap. docs/ROADMAP.md 02-collector-schema notes require it explicitly: \"A gap beyond `collection.max_collection_gap_minutes` (90) means plays may already have been lost silently and with a bias toward the heaviest listening days \u2014 the Collector checks itself against that bound and warns.\" The default is already present in config.py:43 (`collection: {max_collection_gap_minutes: 90}`) and is unread by any code on this branch (grep for max_collection_gap_minutes matches config.py only). Concrete input: db.latest_played_at(conn,'b') returns a timestamp 5 hours before `now` (timer was down, laptop asleep); collect() computes after_ms from it, stores whatever the 50-item window still holds, returns an int, and emits nothing. The operator gets no signal that plays were irrecoverably dropped \u2014 which is the one failure mode docs/PLAN.md \u00a76 says is silent, unrecoverable, and biased toward the highest-signal days. Compare now-latest_played_at against the configured bound and warn when it is exceeded.; spotify.recent",
